<title>SRI LANKA: Ahungalla up 5 pct on tourism revival.</title>
<headline>Ahungalla up 5 pct on tourism revival.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Ahungalla Hotels Ltd rose five percent or 2.25 rupees to 47.25 early on Thursday, due to an expected revival in tourism, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;With tourism showing signs of turning around, the company is seen doing well in 1997,&quot; said a broker.</p>
<p>The company, a subsidiary of the blue chip Aitken Spence &amp; Co, owns and manages about nine hotels in Sri Lanka and the Maldives.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
